  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Let a (x,y)(x, y)(x,y) rectangle denote an axis-aligned rectangle with width equal to xxx and height equal to yyy, where xxx and yyy are positive integers.\n\nYou are given a (N,M)(N, M)(N,M) rectangle. You must repeat the following process as long as your rectangle has at least one side longer than 111:\n\n\nMake a horizontal or vertical cut inside the rectangle, splitting it into two rectangles. The sides of both these rectangles must still be positive integers.\nIf the cut is horizontal, discard the bottom rectangle, otherwise discard the right rectangle. The process continues with the remaining rectangle.\nIn the end, you are left with a (1,1)(1, 1)(1,1) rectangle --- a square with side length 111.\n\nThere may be several possible ways or paths to reduce a (N,M)(N, M)(N,M) rectangle to a (1,1)(1,1)(1,1) rectangle. Let's define the cost of a path as the sum of areas of all rectangles present in that path, including the (N,M)(N,M)(N,M) and (1,1)(1,1)(1,1) rectangle.\n\nFor example, let's consider a (2,2)(2,2)(2,2) rectangle. There are two possible paths to reduce a (2,2)(2,2)(2,2) rectangle to a (1,1)(1,1)(1,1) rectangle:\n\n\n(2,2)→(1,2)→(1,1)(2,2) \\rightarrow (1,2) \\rightarrow (1,1)(2,2)→(1,2)→(1,1)\n(2,2)→(2,1)→(1,1)(2,2) \\rightarrow (2,1) \\rightarrow (1,1)(2,2)→(2,1)→(1,1)\nThe cost of the first path is 2⋅2+1⋅2+1⋅1=72 \\cdot 2 + 1 \\cdot 2 + 1 \\cdot 1 = 72⋅2+1⋅2+1⋅1=7, and similarly, the cost of the second path is 2⋅2+2⋅1+1⋅1=72 \\cdot 2 + 2 \\cdot 1 + 1 \\cdot 1 = 72⋅2+2⋅1+1⋅1=7.\n\nYou are also given a known prime number PPP. Find the sum of costs of all possible paths modulo PPP.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first and only line of each test case contains three space-separated integers NNN, MMM and PPP.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print a single line containing one integer --- the sum of costs of all paths modulo PPP.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤4,0001 \\leq T \\leq 4,0001≤T≤4,000",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤M≤1081 \\leq M \\leq 10^81≤M≤108",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10510^5105",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask #1 (20 points):**",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 1,0001,0001,000",
